      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "Render a Knowledge Graph to GitHub Pages",
      "summary": "Render a Knowledge Graph — the whole of it, or a list of its Subgraphs — to GitHub Pages at a publication root URL, and report the push: a STATUS (pushed, not pushed, could not determine) and one MESSAGE carrying the deployed commit and the QA result.",
      "description": "Render a Knowledge Graph — the whole of it, or a list of its Subgraphs — to GitHub Pages at a publication root URL, and report the push: a STATUS (pushed, not pushed, could not determine) and one MESSAGE carrying the deployed commit and the QA result.\n\nbranches/ AND RELEASE ARE THE SAME PROCESS. A preview is this with a root under the release root; a release is this with the release root. What differs between them — who may start it, what must be reviewed first, what else lives on the same host — belongs to whatever calls this, never in here.\n\nEVERY STEP IS ONE OF THESE TOOLS: site.ts stages, site.ts --check and readme-book.ts --check check the staging, publish-site.ts deploys, pages-status.ts checks what is served and writes the message. The skill render-kg-to-github-pages has each command.\n\nTHREE STATES, NOT TWO. A check that could not look (a 403 from a proxy, no network) is could-not-determine, and never reported as pushed.\n\nisExecutable is false and no activity carries a work-plan element: this diagram is in bootstrap's diagram vocabulary, which has none.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/render-kg-to-github-pages.bpmn",
